# The Aether release fbs-core is built and tested against.
#
# A FLOOR, not a preference: the oldest Aether that can compile this
# repo's sources and run its suite. Anything newer on PATH is used as-is.
#
# Why 0.542.0 — the port's test suite is `std.spec` (+
# `std.http.client.httptest`), the stdlib absorption of the retired
# aeocha framework. `std.spec` landed in 0.538.0 and the process/HTTP
# matcher modules alongside it, so 0.538.0 is the language floor; we pin
# to 0.542.0 because that is the release the suite is verified green on,
# and because 0.541.0 carries the weak-`aether_lib_meta` fix that aeb's
# multi-TU `--emit=lib` link shape needs (see aeb's own AETHER_PIN).
#
# Bump when this repo starts calling a primitive an older Aether lacks.
#
# Raised 0.542.0 -> 0.778.0 (2026-10-05). A TRACKING/policy move to the
# family-wide floor every Aether repo moved to the same day -- but one that
# the code now genuinely needs, because the port had to change to build:
#
#   1. Aether 0.758 (#2301): the byte-payload std calls take a `byte[]` slice
#      (the length travels with it) instead of (ptr/string, len) pairs.
#      fbs-core calls the slice forms of fs.write_atomic / fs.pwrite,
#      cryptography.md5_hex / sha256_hex / hmac_sha256_hex /
#      hmac_sha256_bytes / digest_update and http client set_body
#      (string.bytes(s), or string.aether_string_raw_ptr(p) as byte[] bounded
#      by an explicit length where the body is http.request_body's raw char*
#      that can hold NULs), so it CANNOT COMPILE below 0.758.
#   2. 0.612: spec.run_summary returns its verdict instead of exiting; the
#      suites now `return spec.run_summary(fw)` so a failing spec exits
#      non-zero (the bare call was measured exiting 0 on a failing spec).
#      On an ae below 0.612 that return hands main() garbage.
#   3. 0.741 (#2208): release installs ship contrib/, so `import
#      contrib.sqlite` resolves from a get.sh toolchain with no aether source
#      checkout. (The veneer archive it links, -laether_sqlite, is still not
#      shipped: scripts/sqlite_veneer.sh builds it from that contrib source.)
#
# So the code's own minimum is now 0.758.0; 0.778.0 is the family floor and
# the release it is verified on (macOS arm64): ./build.sh builds the server,
# scripts/aetest.sh runs all 19 suites green (94 specs + large_sizes, the
# same as 0.542.0 gave on the pre-port code), and a real server round trip
# (bootstrap, bucket, PUT/GET/HEAD/LIST/copy/multipart/DELETE) matches 0.542.
0.778.0
